{"_id":"68a736108ec3d8323af13bc8","roadmapSlug":"cyber-security","nodeId":"WG7DdsxESm31VcLFfkVTz","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:56.577Z","description":"# Authentication vs. Authorization\n\nAuthentication verifies who a user is, confirming their identity using credentials like usernames and passwords. Authorization, on the other hand, determines what a user is allowed to access after they've been authenticated. In essence, authentication proves you are who you say you are, while authorization dictates what you can do.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Two-factor authentication (2FA)","url":"https://authy.com/what-is-2fa/","_id":"6a7f4a39cb44947debcf4d72"},{"type":"article","title":"Biometrics (fingerprint, facial recognition, etc.)","url":"https://me-en.kaspersky.com/resource-center/definitions/biometrics","_id":"6a7f4a39cb44947debcf4d73"},{"type":"article","title":"Security tokens or certificates","url":"https://www.comodo.com/e-commerce/ssl-certificates/certificate.php","_id":"6a7f4a39cb44947debcf4d74"},{"type":"article","title":"Role-based access control (RBAC)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Role-based_access_control","_id":"6a7f4a39cb44947debcf4d75"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:02:49.638Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/cyber-security/content/WG7DdsxESm31VcLFfkVTz.md"}